From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: what an opaque DC render target reads from its DC reaches DXVK too

0807 made an opaque ID2D1DCRenderTarget start from what its DC shows: at
BeginDraw the DC's pixels are copied with GDI into the DC of the target's
surface (IDXGISurface1::GetDC). That DC was released with an empty dirty
rectangle, which says nothing was drawn. Wine's own Direct3D ignores the
rectangle, so the gates passed; DXVK -- the Direct3D of every Stained
Glass OS installation -- honours it and kept the surface as it was:
black. Paint.NET 5 drew its menus as black boxes in which the items that
have a shortcut showed only the shortcut (their names are drawn in a
second pass through such a target), and its Colors window's "More >>"
button was blank (regression walk 2026-10-05, item 45).

The surface's DC is now released with no rectangle: the whole surface is
dirty, as GDI drew all of it.

Test: test/dcrtdxvk-gate.sh (test/dcrt-opaque-probe.cpp over DXVK's
d3d11/dxgi; mutant SG_MUTANT_DCRT_EMPTY_DIRTY). dcrt-opaque-gate still
passes.
---
--- a/dlls/d2d1/dc_render_target.c
+++ b/dlls/d2d1/dc_render_target.c
@@ -840,7 +840,9 @@
 {
     struct d2d_dc_render_target *render_target = impl_from_IUnknown(outer_unknown);
     const RECT *r = &render_target->dst_rect;
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_DCRT_EMPTY_DIRTY
     RECT empty_rect;
+#endif
     HDC dst_hdc;
 
     if (render_target->desc.pixelFormat.alphaMode == D2D1_ALPHA_MODE_PREMULTIPLIED)
@@ -856,8 +858,15 @@
     if (SUCCEEDED(IDXGISurface1_GetDC(render_target->dxgi_surface, FALSE, &dst_hdc)))
     {
         BitBlt(dst_hdc, 0, 0, r->right - r->left, r->bottom - r->top, render_target->hdc, r->left, r->top, SRCCOPY);
+        /* What GDI drew is kept: the whole surface is dirty. An empty dirty
+         * rectangle says nothing was drawn, and a Direct3D that honours it
+         * (DXVK, every installation's) keeps the old contents -- black. */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DCRT_EMPTY_DIRTY
+        IDXGISurface1_ReleaseDC(render_target->dxgi_surface, NULL);
+#else
         SetRectEmpty(&empty_rect);
         IDXGISurface1_ReleaseDC(render_target->dxgi_surface, &empty_rect);
+#endif
     }
 #endif
 }
